<p>From Test 1 (with <code>@tailwindcss/vite@4.2</code> what supports Vite 8), it's clear that no warning appears when everything is correct.</p>
<p>From Test 2 (with <code>@tailwindcss/vite@4.1</code> what doesn't support Vite 8), it shows that if the Vite version is indeed incompatible, the warning still remains only for the relevant cases.</p>

Q: How to convert JsonNode to Map A: <p>Change the type reference to use the <code>Map</code> interface instead of the <code>HashMap</code> class. So <code>new TypeReference&lt;Map&lt;String, Object&gt;&gt;</code>.</p>

<p>Update:<br>
Also, you said your JSON node has the value <code>"{\"id\":\"bar\"}"</code>. That's not a JSON object, that's a JSON string. Ensure your whole object looks like this:</p>

<pre><code>{
  "variables": {
    "id":"bar"
  },
  "otherFields": ...
}
</code></pre>

<p>and not like this:</p>

<pre><code>{
  "variables": "{\"id\":\"bar\"}",
  "otherFields": ...
}
</code></pre>

Q: Could not load file or assembly &#39;Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestPlatform.ObjectModel, Version=11.0.0.0&#39; A: <p>Same issue, I was able to install the latest version:</p>
<pre><code>Install-Package Microsoft.TestPlatform.ObjectModel -Version 15.8.0
</code></pre>
<p>Then add a binding redirect to the test projects app.config:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>    &lt;runtime&gt;
        &lt;assemblyBinding xmlns=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1&quot;&gt;
            &lt;dependentAssembly&gt;
                &lt;assemblyIdentity name=&quot;Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestPlatform.ObjectModel&quot; publicKeyToken=&quot;b03f5f7f11d50a3a&quot; culture=&quot;neutral&quot; /&gt;
                &lt;bindingRedirect oldVersion=&quot;11.0.0.0-14.0.0.0&quot; newVersion=&quot;15.0.0.0&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;/dependentAssembly&gt;
        &lt;/assemblyBinding&gt;
    &lt;/runtime&gt;
</code></pre>
